  "question": {
    "text": "On reaction with stronger oxidizing agent like <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>KIO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>, hydrogen peroxide oxidizes with the evolution of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>. The oxidation number of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math> in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>KIO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> changes to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "5",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Hydrogen peroxide&nbsp;acts as an oxidising as well as reducing agent in both acidic and alkaline media.</p><p>But its reducing action is more effective in alkaline medium</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>KIO</mi><mn>4</mn><mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><msubsup><mi>KIO</mi><mn>3</mn><mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math></p><p>The oxidation number of iodine in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>IO</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup></math>&nbsp;is +5</p><p>The geometry of iodine containing compound changes from tetrahedral to pyramidal in the above reaction</p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
